[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m The numerator is \( (n^3 + 3n)^2 \). We can factor it as:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \[ n^3 + 3n = n(n^2 + 3) \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m so,
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \[ (n^3 + 3n)^2 = (n(n^2 + 3))^2 = n^2 (n^2 + 3)^2 \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m The denominator is \( n^6 - 64 \). This is a difference of squares, which factors to:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \[ n^6 - 64 = (n^3)^2 - 8^2 = (n^3 - 8)(n^3 + 8) \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m Since \( n^3 - 8 \) and \( n^3 + 8 \) are both differences and sums of cubes, we can further factor them:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \[ n^3 - 8 = (n-2)(n^2 + 2n + 4) \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \[ n^3 + 8 = (n+2)(n^2 - 2n + 4) \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m So,
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \[ n^6 - 64 = (n-2)(n^2 + 2n + 4)(n+2)(n^2 - 2n + 4) \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
