[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m Please answer the following question: Read the following article and select the best answer. Article: If the only sports you do are in P.E.class,then you might only think of sports as something you do once or twice a week. _ fact,experts recommend that everyone should get at least 30 minutes of moderate   physical activity almost every day.Keeping physically fit isn't just for the good of enjoyment.There are lots of good reasons for working out.It can help you: *have stronger muscles and bones *keep a healthier weight *lower your cholesterol   and blood pressure level *feel better about yourself *set a good example for your friends and family Members *get higher scores on tests and benefit your grades *keep the risk of smoking and drinking low Teens should get 60 minutes of moderate physical activity on most days of the week.Working out shouldn't be a job,but part of the fun of life.Remember: *Exercise with other people. *Don't work out so much that you aren't as fun to be with. *Don't overdo it.If you're exercising so much that you feel sick,tired,or stressed,you'll have a hard time keeping it up.Choose activities that are fun.Not only will you enjoy them more,but you'll be more likely to keep doing them. *If you're not used to much physical activity,check with your doctor before you start a fitness program. Question: According to the passage,which of the following is not the advantage for teens to do sports? - It'll help them keep physically fit. - It can help teens stay away from cigarettes and alcohol. - It might lower teens' level of knowledge. - It can help them feel better about themselves.
