[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m Please answer the following question: Read the following article and select the best answer. Article: In fact, the most important words in any language are the small words. They are the ones we use all the time. For example, here are five of the most common words in English: the, of, and, to, a. And here are five of the most common helping verbs: am, have, be, do, will. Some people go from place to place, speaking very few words. These people are not necessarily shy. They may just be missing some of the small words they need in the sentences to communicate well. They don't speak English as English speakers do. When they learn some of these common small words and use them in sentences, they will probably be able to express their ideas more clearly than before, and they will find they are better able to express themselves all the way around. People who use a little vocabulary, but who have mastered the small words and helping verbs can express their ideas faster and better than people with a large vocabulary but who have done little work on how to actually put small words together in order to form sentences to express their ideas. They can learn many _ by reading out loud and saying the words over and over again until they own them. With practice, something that sounded strange at first suddenly sounds right to their ears. Whether they write it or say it, the language starts to flow better. So if you want to learn English language, start with small words. You should master the small words and short sentence patterns so that you can put together the words or use the patterns to share your ideas with others. Question: If you master some common small words, you   _  . Options: A: will only learn English faster B: won't be able to express themselves better when you learn more new words C: only develop your listening skills well D: can express your ideas better than others who master some new words
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m A:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m D: can express your ideas better than others who master some new words
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m Please answer the following question: Read the following article and select the best answer. Article: In late May, after 24 hours to fly from New Zealand to Los Angeles, I was pretty wiped out. Just as I was thinking of relaxing myself in my hotel room, a call came in. "Hi, my name is George. It's 11 o'clock Tuesday night. There is a boat at the Northridge Golf Club  with a sailboat in the water. Can you come, please?" Sleepy as I was, I didn't want to miss my chance. I jumped out of my car and drove to the golf club with George, leaving my hotel behind. It turned out that the sailboat was a new one, and its owner was a woman from Sweden. The woman didn't know about the wind. I don't know how it went, but it ended up in the Northridge Golf Club. At first I had some doubt if I could rescue the boat by myself, but George said he could do something and he ordered some people to get to work. With the club pro and a few golfers, we managed to pull the sailboat out in an hour. Everyone seemed really happy. But I was too tired to enjoy the success. _ I felt like I needed a week to sleep. But as I went back to my hotel, I felt very proud of having taken part in this event. This was a great story to start my own sailing rescuing stories in the U.S. Though I was tired, I was still very glad, because it gave me some confidence . After that, as a sailing rescuer, I felt I should take more responsibility to give a hand to people in need. Even more, I got to know that I wasn't a stranger in this country and I was connected with it. Question: What might be the best title for this passage? Options: A: A Beautiful Story B: A Tiring Job C: An Important Rescue D: My First American Rescue
