[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 1. **Convert \( 17_b \) and \( 97_b \) to base 10:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( 17_b \) in base 10 is \( 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7 \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( 97_b \) in base 10 is \( 9 \cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7 \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 2. **Set up the divisibility condition:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - We need \( b + 7 \) to be a divisor of \( 9b + 7 \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 3. **Express the divisibility condition mathematically:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7} \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 4. **Simplify the congruence:**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( 9b + 7 = k(b + 7) \) for some integer \( k \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( 9b + 7 = kb + 7k \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( 9b - kb = 7k - 7 \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( b(9 - k) = 7(k - 1) \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 5. **Solve for \( b \):**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( b = \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 6. **Find integer solutions for \( b \):**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( b \) must be an integer, so \( \frac{7(k - 1)}{9 - k} \) must be an integer.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - This implies that \( 9 - k \) must be a divisor of \( 7(k - 1) \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 7. **Check possible values of \( k \):**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( k = 10 \): \( b = \frac{7(10 - 1)}{9 - 10} = \frac{63}{-1} = -63 \) (not valid since \( b > 9 \)).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-3) pid=21766, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    - \( k = 8 \): \( b = \frac{7(8 - 1)}{9 - 8} = \frac{49}{1} = 49 \)
