[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 2. **Find the cumulative distribution function (CDF) of \( V \):**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    The CDF of \( V \) is given by:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    F_V(v) = P(V \leq v) = P(XY \leq v).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    We need to consider the region in the \( xy \)-plane where \( xy \leq v \). This region is a hyperbola \( y = \frac{v}{x} \) for \( 0 < v < 1 \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    For \( 0 < v < 1 \), the region where \( xy \leq v \) is bounded by the lines \( y = 0 \), \( x = 1 \), \( y = 1 \), and the hyperbola \( y = \frac{v}{x} \). We can integrate the joint PDF over this region:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    F_V(v) = \int_0^1 \int_0^{v/x} 1 \, dy \, dx = \int_0^1 \frac{v}{x} \, dx = v \int_0^1 \frac{1}{x} \, dx.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    However, we need to split the integral into two parts because the hyperbola \( y = \frac{v}{x} \) intersects the line \( y = 1 \) at \( x = v \):
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    F_V(v) = \int_0^v \int_0^1 1 \, dy \, dx + \int_v^1 \int_0^{v/x} 1 \, dy \, dx = \int_0^v 1 \, dx + \int_v^1 \frac{v}{x} \, dx = v + v \int_v^1 \frac{1}{x} \, dx = v + v \left[ \ln x \right]_v^1 = v + v (\ln 1 - \ln v) = v - v \ln v.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    For \( v \geq 1 \), \( F_V(v) = 1 \) because \( V \) can never be greater than 1.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 3. **Find the PDF of \( V \):**
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    The PDF of \( V \) is the derivative of the CDF with respect to \( v \):
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    f_V(v) = \frac{d}{dv} F_V(v) = \frac{d}{dv} (v - v \ln v) = 1 - \ln v - 1 = -\ln v \quad \text{for} \quad 0 < v < 1.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m    For \( v \geq 1 \), \( f_V(v) = 0 \).
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m Therefore, the PDF of \( V \) is:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m f_V(v) = -\ln v \quad \text{for} \quad 0 < v < 1.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \]
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m 
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m The final answer is:
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \[
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \boxed{-\ln v \text{ for } 0 < v < 1}.
[36m(MathRuleRewardWorker(reward-math_rule-1) pid=21765, ip=10.17.70.33)[0m \]
